coring potential and best tile efficiency given my current hand structure.\n\nReason: B5 is the only non-Bamboo suited tile disrupting a potential Full Flush pattern. With predominantly Bamboo tiles (T3-T9) and an exposed Bamboo chow [T1-T2-T3], pursuing Full Flush (24 points) provides the clearest path to a winning hand worth 8+ points. The remaining Bamboo tiles form multiple sequential combinations with reasonable availability in unshown tiles.\n\nAnswer: Play B5"}
